1.  `When you have give a range and in that range for different queries you have to return number of divisors` : Then 
    precompute them for efficient usage look the code below for better understanding.
    
    
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
const int N = 1e6;
int cnt[N+1];

void calculate(){

   
    for(int i = 1 ; i <= N ; i++){
        for(int j = i ; j <= N ; j += i){
            cnt[j]++;
        }
    }
}


void solve(){
     int n;
    cin >> n;
    cout << cnt[n] << '\n';
}

int main(){

    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(0);cin.tie(0);
    calculate();
    int t;
    cin >> t;
    while(t--){
    solve();
    }
    return 0;
}


2. `Printing a number into a small letter character` : `cout << char(x+'a') << '\';` considering that x is a number less than equal to 25.


3. `Storing any lexogrphically shorter string in a string` : `string s = min(r,p);` this will store lexographically shorter string in string s.


4. `Modern c++ way to create a static array` : `array<int,26> cnt {}` by this we created a cnt array of 26 elements and initialized all 26 
    elements of array cnt as default value (and default value for int is 0) . 
    
	1. This is modern c++ object type
	2. `Value initialization` : `{}` initialize all elements as 0.
	3. `size` : `cnt.size()`
	4. `Passing to Functions` : value and reference both are possible . 
	5. `It suppors almost all functions of vector array` : like comparing two arrays directly `a == b` check element by element 
	6. `sorting` : `sort(cnt.begin(),cnt.end());` 
	7. `iterators` : `.begin(),.end(),.rbegin(),r.end()`
	8. `2d array` : `array <array <int,3> 3> grid{};` 
	
	
5. `What is recursion ` : a function which calls itself that function is known as recurssive function. Recursion runs for infinite 
    times until we didn't break intentionally or return a segmentation fault , we get segmentation fault as internal implementation
    of recursion is done using stacks and stack stores memory of functions address because recurssion will refer previously called 
    function's address and our computer allocate a particular space for stack and when that space get filled we get segmentation 
    fault and not tle  and we get segmentation fault whenever we have any issue around memory.
    
    
6. `Base condition in a recurssive function` : We write this in order to terminate our recurssive function and we place base condition 
    before the recurssive condition. 
    
    	   #include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;


void func(int n){
    if (n==0) return;
    func(n-1);
}

int main(){

    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(0);cin.tie(0);
    func(5);
    return 0;
}
    
    
7. `Demonstration of how recurssion actually works with a example below` : Below we have a recurssive function and there will be a 
    difference that if we doing tasks before the calling the function again or after calling the function there will be difference
    between them like below i did printing n after calling recurssive function then this will work as first run for `fucn(5)` --> 
    `func(4)` --> `func(3)` --> `func(2)` --> `func(1)`  and as the our function sees next functions call this will run till only 
    line 3 and in then n will get 0 and this start returning and as current stack condition is `12345` (i written stack as left to
    right as top to bottom) so then return will call first `fucn(1)` --> `func(2)` --> `func(3)` --> `func(4)` --> `func(5)` and
    once this sees return now functions will run for the rest of lines means for line number 4 , 5 and get ended now this will
    print n means we will get output `12345` and if write `cout << n << '\n';` before `funct(n-1)` then we will get `54321` as
    output stack will be still same because while returning the function we are printing nothing.
    
       #include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;


void func(int n){ // line 1.
    if (n==0) return; // line 2. 
    func(n-1); // line 3. 
    cout << n << '\n'; // line 4.
} // line 5.

int main(){

    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(0);cin.tie(0);
    func(5);
    return 0;
}


8. `Accessing all characters of a string in a loop with auto method` : `for(auto c:s){ cout << c << ' ';}` we will get all elements 
    from string s. And this thing even work for most of such related things like vectors , sets etc. This is modern method to print
    characters out of a string.
